tinal ganglion cell with synaptic terminals in S4 that is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21514:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003042 \"M9-OFF retinal ganglion cell\")\n21519:# Class: obo:CL_0003043 (M10 retinal ganglion cell)\n21521:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003043 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and large dendritic field, with dense dendritic arbor.\")\n21526:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003043 \"M10 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21531:# Class: obo:CL_0003044 (M11 retinal ganglion cell)\n21533:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003044 \"A bistratified ganglion cell with small, dense dendritic fields that terminate in S1 and S3.\")\n21538:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003044 \"M11 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21545:# Class: obo:CL_0003045 (M12 retinal ganglion cell)\n21547:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003045 \"A bistratified ganglion cell with larger, asymetric dendritic fields that terminate in S2 and S4.\")\n21552:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003045 \"M12 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21559:# Class: obo:CL_0003046 (M13 retinal ganglion cell)\n21561:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003046 \"A bistratifed retinal ganglion cell that has small, symmetric dendritic fields that terminate in S2 and S4.\")\n21566:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003046 \"M13 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21573:# Class: obo:CL_0003047 (M14 retinal ganglion cell)\n21575:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003047 \"A bistratifed retinal ganglion cell that has small, symmetric dendritic fields that terminate in S1 and S4-S5.\")\n21580:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003047 \"M14 retinal ganglion cell\")\n21654:# Class: obo:CL_0004115 (retinal ganglion cell B)\n21656:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004115 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with small to medium soma and small to medium dendritic field.\")\n21661:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004115 \"retinal ganglion cell B\")\n21666:# Class: obo:CL_0004116 (retinal ganglion cell C)\n21668:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004116 \"A retinal ganglion with cell medium cell bodies and medium to large dendritic fields.\")\n21674:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004116 \"retinal ganglion cell C\")\n21678:# Class: obo:CL_0004117 (retinal ganglion cell A)\n21680:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004117 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with large soma and large dendritic field.\")\n21688:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004117 \"retinal ganglion cell A\")\n21693:# Class: obo:CL_0004119 (retinal ganglion cell B1)\n21695:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004119 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has medium body size, medium dendritic field and dense dendritic arbor, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21699:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004119 \"retinal ganglion cell B4\")\n21703:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004119 \"retinal ganglion cell B1\")\n21707:# Class: obo:CL_0004120 (retinal ganglion cell A1)\n21709:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004120 \"A retinal ganglion A cell found in the retina with large somata, often polygonal in shape. The dendritic fields consist of three to seven stout dendrites that are sparce near soma. Dendrites terminate in S4.\")\n21714:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004120 \"inner alpha retinal ganglion cell\")\n21718:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004120 \"retinal ganglion cell A1\")\n21722:# Class: obo:CL_0004121 (retinal ganglion cell B2)\n21724:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004121 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has a very small but very dense dendritic field, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21730:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004121 \"retinal ganglion cell B2\")\n21734:# Class: obo:CL_0004124 (retinal ganglion cell C1)\n21736:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004124 \"A retinal ganglion cell C inner that has medium dendritic diversity.\")\n21745:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004124 \"retinal ganglion cell C1\")\n21748:# Class: obo:CL_0004125 (retinal ganglion cell C2 inner)\n21750:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004125 \"A retinal ganglion cell C inner that has dense dendritic diversity.\")\n21756:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004125 \"retinal ganglion cell C2 inner\")\n21759:# Class: obo:CL_0004126 (retinal ganglion cell C2 outer)\n21761:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004126 \"A retinal ganglion cell C outer that has symmetrical and dense dendritic dendritic tree with a large dendritic field.\")\n21767:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004126 \"retinal ganglion cell C2 outer\")\n21770:# Class: obo:CL_0004137 (retinal ganglion cell A2 inner)\n21772:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004137 \"A retinal ganglion A2 cell with dendrites terminating in S4.\")\n21778:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004137 \"retinal ganglion cell A2 inner\")\n21782:# Class: obo:CL_0004138 (retinal ganglion cell A2)\n21784:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004138 \"A retinal ganglion A cell with dense arbor near soma.\")\n21787:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0004138 \"outer alpha retinal ganglion cell\")\n21792:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004138 \"retinal ganglion cell A2\")\n21795:# Class: obo:CL_0004139 (retinal ganglion cell A2 outer)\n21797:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004139 \"A retinal ganglion A2 cell with dendrites terminating in S2.\")\n21803:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004139 \"retinal ganglion cell A2 outer\")\n21830:# Class: obo:CL_0004183 (retinal ganglion cell B3)\n21832:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004183 \"A monostratified retinal ganglion cell with medium soma, sparse dendritic tree, and medium dendritic field.\")\n21839:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004183 \"retinal ganglion cell B3\")\n21866:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004215 \"A type 5 cone bipolar cell with narrowly stratified post synaptic terminals.\")\n22001:# Class: obo:CL_0004226 (monostratified amacrine cell)\n22008:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004226 \"monostratified amacrine cell\")\n22013:# Class: obo:CL_0004227 (flat bistratified amacrine cell)\n22015:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25630271\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004227 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field. Flat bistratified amacrine cells have post-synaptic terminals both on the border of S1 and S2, and on the border of S3 and S4. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n22020:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004227 \"flat bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22043:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004229 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field that has dendrite stratification in S2, and in S3 and S4.\")\n22054:# Class: obo:CL_0004230 (diffuse bistratified amacrine cell)\n22056:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004230 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field that has post-synaptic terminals in S1 and the border of S1-S2, and termination of a second arbor within the border of S2-S3 and S3.\")\n22061:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004230 \"diffuse bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22109:# Class: obo:CL_0004234 (diffuse multistratified amacrine cell)\n22116:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004234 \"diffuse multistratified amacrine cell\")\n22163:# Class: obo:CL_0004238 (asymmetric bistratified amacrine cell)\n22165:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004238 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field, a flat and sparse dendritic arbor, and post-synaptic terminals at the intersections of S1 and S2, and S3 and S4.\")\n22170:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004238 \"asymmetric bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22176:# Class: obo:CL_0004239 (wavy bistratified amacrine cell)\n22178:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004239 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S1-S2, and S4.\")\n22183:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004239 \"wavy bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22258:# Class: obo:CL_0004246 (monostratified cell)\n22265:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004246 \"monostratified cell\")\n22268:# Class: obo:CL_0004247 (bistratified cell)\n22274:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004247 \"bistratified cell\")\n22278:# Class: obo:CL_0004250 (bistratified retinal amacrine cell)\n22285:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004250 \"bistratified retinal amacrine cell\")\n23903:# Class: obo:CL_0009066 (stratified squamous epithelial cell of anal canal)\n23905:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009066 \"A stratified squamous epithelial cell that is part of the anal canal.\")\n23907:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009066 \"anal canal stratified squamous epithelial cell\")\n23910:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009066 \"stratified squamous epithelial cell of anal canal\")\n24214:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11694559\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009096 \"Any cell that is part of the esophageal non-keratinized stratified squamous epithelium. In humans, the esophagus, which requires flexibility to accommodate swallowing of a bolus, is covered with a non-keratinized epithelium.\")\n24449:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/417>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2478566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28445731\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30420661\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010000 \"A differentiating matrix keratinocyte that has initiated terminal differentiation and keratin synthesis. This cell undergoes a characteristic change while migrating upward from the hair follicle bulb, representing a committed progenitor cell destined to form the hair medulla, cortex and hair root sheath.\")\n25569:# Class: obo:CL_1000083 (stratified keratinized epithelial stem cell)\n25571:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1000083 \"stratified keratinized epithelial stem cell\")\n25574:# Class: obo:CL_1000085 (stratified non keratinized epithelial stem cell)\n25576:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1000085 \"stratified non keratinized epithelial stem cell\")\n29325:# Class: obo:CL_2000050 (obsolete retina retinal ganglion cell)\n29327:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000050 \"Any retinal ganglion cell that is part of a retina.\")\n29332:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000050 \"obsolete retina retinal ganglion cell\")\n29469:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12052228\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15749958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23467088\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31672973\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000064 \"A meso-epithelial cell of the ovarian surface epithelium, varying in shape from flat to cuboidal to pseudostratified columnar. This cell plays a crucial role in ovulation by producing proteolytic enzymes in response to gonadotropins, facilitating follicle rupture through tissue breakdown and TNF-alpha signaling. Additionally, this cell contributes to post-ovulatory wound repair (Morris et al., 2022) and exhibits stem cell-like properties (Flesken-Nikitin et al., 2013; Wang et al., 2019).\")\n30241:# Class: obo:CL_4023032 (ON retinal ganglion cell)\n30244:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19602302\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023032 \"A retinal ganglion cell that is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n30245:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023032 \"ON retinal ganglion cell\")\n30248:# Class: obo:CL_4023033 (OFF retinal ganglion cell)\n30250:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19602302\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023033 \"A retinal ganglion cell that is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center.\")\n30252:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023033 \"OFF retinal ganglion cell\")\n31290:# Class: obo:CL_4023188 (midget ganglion cell of retina)\n31292:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Midget_cell&oldid=982299713\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023188 \"A retinal ganglion cell that originate in the ganglion cell layer of the retina, and project to the parvocellular layers of the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). These cells are known as midget retinal ganglion cells due to the small sizes of their dendritic trees and cell bodies.\")\n31295:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023188 \"There are midget bipolar cells of retina and midget ganglion cells of retina and they are not the same:\n31297:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023188 \"midget ganglion cell of retina\")\n31301:# Class: obo:CL_4023189 (parasol ganglion cell of retina)\n31303:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Parasol_cell&oldid=1032171532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023189 \"A retinal ganglion cell located in the ganglion cell layer of the retina. This cell projects to magnocellular cells in the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). They have large cell bodies and extensive, branching dendritic networks that contribute to their large receptive fields.\")\n31308:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023189 \"These cells should not be confused with M1-M14 retinal ganglion cells described in PMID:16626866 which refer to a different classification of retinal ganglion cells.\")\n31309:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023189 \"parasol ganglion cell of retina\")\n31648:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30069044\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030024 \"An epithelial, transitional cell type between basal and secretory; located in stratified, non-ciliated structures (called hillocks) with high cell turnover in epithelium. In some mammalian species, this cell type has been noted to express KRT13 and is postulated to play a role in squamous barrier function and immunomodulation.\")\n32295:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033019 \"The axons of a blue cone bipolar cell terminate close to the ganglion cell layer, where they transfer the S-cone ON signal to small bistratified ganglion cells. Other targets of a blue cone bipolar cell include amacrine cells and possibly large bistratified ganglion cells.\")\n32376:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22006647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033027 \"In primates, a diffuse bipolar 1 cell on average makes 81 ribbon (output) synapses, 13 contacts are with OFF parasol cells and 47 contacts are with OFF midget cells. This cell might make flat contacts at both triad-associated and non-triad-associated positions on the cone pedicle.\")\n32382:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25309346\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26500507\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033028 \"An OFF diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells. This cell contains a large number of synaptic ribbons and a small axon arbor area.\")\n32386:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033028 \"In primates, a diffuse bipolar 2 cell makes an average of 133 ribbon synapses, 47 contacts are with OFF parasol cells and 4 contacts are with OFF midget cells.\")\n32397:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033029 \"Originally, DB3a cells were termed diffuse bipolar 3 (DB3) cells. When an additional bipolar type which stratifies slightly more vitread and is calbindin negative was detected, this cell was renamed diffuse bipolar 3a cell. The axons of neighboring DB3a cells make homologous gap junctions. The DB3a cells provide the majority of their output to OFF parasol cells.\")\n32413:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033031 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells.\")\n32429:# Class: obo:CL_4033033 (flat midget bipolar cell)\n32435:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033033 \"flat midget bipolar cell\")\n32438:# Class: obo:CL_4033034 (invaginating midget bipolar cell)\n32444:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033034 \"invaginating midget bipolar cell\")\n32453:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033035 \"A giant bipolar cell is usually monostratified, although, very rarely, it can be bistratified.\")\n32568:# Class: obo:CL_4033046 (ON midget ganglion cell)\n32570:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033046 \"A midget ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to increased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from invaginating midget bipolar cells.\")\n32573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033046 \"ON-midget RGC\")\n32574:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033046 \"ON-midget cell\")\n32575:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033046 \"inner stratifying midget cell\")\n32576:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033046 \"ON midget ganglion cell\")\n32579:# Class: obo:CL_4033047 (OFF midget ganglion cell)\n32581:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033047 \"A midget ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to decreased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from flat midget bipolar cells.\")\n32584:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033047 \"OFF-midget RGC\")\n32585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033047 \"OFF-midget cell\")\n32586:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033047 \"outer stratifying midget cell\")\n32587:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033047 \"OFF midget ganglion cell\")\n32624:# Class: obo:CL_4033051 (OFF parasol ganglion cell)\n32626:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033051 \"A parasol ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to decreased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from DB3a bipolar cells.\")\n32629:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol RGC\")\n32630:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF-parasol retinal ganglion cell\")\n32631:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033051 \"outer parasol cell\")\n32632:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033051 \"OFF parasol ganglion cell\")\n32635:# Class: obo:CL_4033052 (ON parasol ganglion cell)\n32637:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033052 \"A parasol ganglion cell that depolarizes in response to increased light intensity in the center of its receptive field. The majority of input that this cell receives comes from DB4 bipolar cells.\")\n32640:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"ON-parasol RGC\")\n32641:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"ON-parasol retinal ganglion cell\")\n32642:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033052 \"inner parasol cell\")\n32643:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033052 \"ON parasol ganglion cell\")\n32646:# Class: obo:CL_4033053 (small bistratified retinal ganglion cell)\n32648:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033053 \"A bistratfied retinal ganglion cell with a small dendritic field that has dendrites in the ON and OFF sublamina of the retinal inner plexiform layer and carries blue-ON/yellow-OFF signals. This cell receives bipolar and amacrine input to both the OFF and ON dendritic tree.\")\n32651:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell\")\n32652:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1002/cne.22183\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell, blue-ON/yellow-OFF ganglion cell\")\n32656:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified retinal ganglion cell\")\n32870:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033085 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that stratifies in the stratum 3 of the inner plexiform layer to make synapses with ON parasol ganglion cells. A diffuse bipolar 5 cell has high expression of MYO16 compared with other bipolar cells.\")\n33556:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35431796\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:3746410\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042038 \"A type of primary motor neuron situated in the rostral region of the spinal cord. RoP neurons extend their axons to innervate the ventral trunk musculature.\")\n33586:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35431796\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:3746410\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042041 \"A type of primary motor neuron located in the middle region of the spinal cord. This primary motor neuron type is characterized by their distinct axonal pathways that innervate the middle trunk muscles.\")\n34565:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28192873\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31194408\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1007/978-3-030-35784-9_2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.5772/intechopen.75538\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052069 \"A duct epithelial cell that is part of the excretory duct of the salivary gland, which transports saliva from the intralobular ductal system to the oral cavity. While primarily serving as a conduit, this cell may play a role in the saliva modification, contributing to its hypotonicity. In humans, this cell has a pseudostratified columnar shape.\")\n35221:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17020902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837987\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32187560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32726565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37672481\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770004 \"An epithelial cell that resides in the layer(s) immediately above the basal layer in stratified or pseudostratified epithelia. This cell mainly originates from basal cells and is found across various tissues, including skin, esophagus, oral mucosa, airway, and cornea.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
