the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is stout and the axon terminates in sublamina 1. The axonal terminal is wide and has only a few varicosities.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000753 \"DB1 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000753 \"type 1 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000753 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000753 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008922))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000753 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000754 (type 2 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000754 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is not well filled and the dendrites are more delicate than in type 1 cells. The axon terminal is bushier and exhibits a dense plexus of varicosities in the inner part of sublamina 1 (Ghosh et al., 2004).  It can be differentiated from other retinal bipolar neurons by its expression of marker genes: Neto1, Lhx3 and Irx-6 (Shekhar, 2016).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000754 \"FMB cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000754 \"type 2 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nEquivalentClasses(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:CL_0000754 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000748 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P50481) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8R4I7) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9ER75)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000754 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000754 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008922))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000754 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000755 (type 3 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000755 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is delicate and the dendritic tips appear small when compared with type 1 cells. The axon terminal is stratified and restricted to sublamina 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000755 \"DB2 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000755 \"type 3 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000755 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000755 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008923))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000755 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000755 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000604))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000756 (type 4 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000756 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a diffuse axon terminal with varicosities in sublaminae 1 and 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000756 \"DB3 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000756 \"type 4 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000756 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000756 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008923))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000756 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008924))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000756 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000756 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000604))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000757 (type 5 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000757 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is restricted to sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer. It is narrowly stratified and branched. The dendritic tree has many delicate branches.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000757 \"DB4 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000757 \"type 5 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000757 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000757 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008924))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000757 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000758 (type 6 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000758 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a loose, delicate axon terminal that opens in sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer and descends into sublamina 4.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000758 \"DB5 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000758 \"type 6 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000758 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000758 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008925))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000758 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000759 (type 7 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000759 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is narrowly stratified and are found just below a calretinin-expressing band in sublamina 4 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000759 \"IMB cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000759 \"type 7 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000759 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000759 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008925))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000759 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000760 (type 8 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000760 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. This cell has the widest dendritic field and the widest axon terminal of all retinal bipolar cells. The axon terminal is delicate and stratified through sublaminae 4 and 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000760 \"DB6 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000760 \"type 8 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000760 obo:CL_0000748)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000760 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008925))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000760 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002102 obo:UBERON_0008926))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000760 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000573))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000761 (type 9 cone bipolar cell (sensu Mus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000761 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is wide and the dendritic convergence indicates cone selectivity. The axon terminal is sparsely branched and terminates in sublamina 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnn